  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/esa-household
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source’s income-attribution provision distinguishes partner income from child or young-person income in the ESA(IR) family context.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol9-ch48/0005
      quote: "48008   In a claim for ESA(IR), the DM should calculate the income of the claimant's partner\n        in the same way as for the claimant1. This income should then be treated as the\n        claimant’s income2. But DMs should consider if the circumstances in DMG 48009 to\n        DMG 48017 applies. Income paid to, or in respect of a child or young person who is\n        a member of the claimant’s family must not be treated as the claimant’s income3.\n        See DMG Chapter 51 for definitions of child, young person and family.\n                                             1 reg 83 (1); 2 WR Act 07, Sch 1, para 6(2); 3 ESA Regs, reg 83(2)\n\n\n\n        Treatment of income - couples"
      locator: DMG 48008
    - page: page/dmg-vol8-ch43/0003
      quote: "43001     This Chapter gives guidance on how to establish membership of a family and\n          membership of the claimant's household for ESA(IR). There is no need for the DM\n          to establish membership of a family and household for ESA(Cont)."
      locator: DMG 43001
